## Learning content — Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International

Learning content in this repository © 2026 The Language Centre, University of
Cambridge, and is licensed under CC BY-NC 4.0.

Full license text: <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/legalcode>
Plain-language summary: <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/>

**You are free to** share the content (copy and redistribute it in any medium
or format, including on your own servers) and adapt it (remix, transform and
build upon it) — **for non-commercial purposes only.**

**Two conditions.**

1. **Attribution.** You must give appropriate credit to The Language Centre,
   University of Cambridge, provide a link to this license, and indicate if you
   made changes. You may do so in any reasonable manner, but not in any way
   that suggests the Language Centre endorses you or your use.
2. **NonCommercial.** You may not use the content for commercial purposes. In
   the words of the license, a commercial use is one "primarily intended for or
   directed toward commercial advantage or monetary compensation."

Attribution is satisfied by, for example:

> Learning content from `French-Basic-2026` © The Language Centre, University of
> Cambridge, licensed under
> [CC BY-NC 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/).
> Modified from the original.

**If you want to use the content commercially,** the NonCommercial term does
not forbid it outright — it means you need separate permission. Ask The Language
Centre, University of Cambridge.

CC BY-NC 4.0 does **not** transfer ownership. Copyright in the content remains
with The Language Centre, University of Cambridge.

Note that the **code is MIT**, which does permit commercial use. The
NonCommercial term applies to the learning content, not to the application
machinery that renders it.

